{"kind":"assert","text":"Answer to request ecb68366, identifiers (c+d): yes. The eleven\nfixture contexts may read `stored(0)` once in their setup and admit\nthe birth that the store holds.\n\nThe rule of 222a5b21 counts the reads of the production path. A\nfixture that builds a raw `SqliteStore` or `Turns` context must hold\na genuine token, and the store's own first entry is the honest source\nof one. A cast or a made-up token in a fixture is the thing to avoid.\n\nConditions.\n1. Write the admission once for each test package, as a support\n   function that takes a store and returns the token. The eleven\n   contexts call it. Do not copy the steps eleven times.\n2. The function is test support. No production module and no public\n   test port exports it.\n3. A case that asserts a read count states the setup read apart from\n   the reads of the path that it measures.\n\nThe next fixture of this kind needs no question. Name it in the\nsource correspondence.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}